      "writtenOn": "2018-07-25T03:44:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So here, this does not make sense, because an int does not have byte order, it\u0027s a value and not a memory reference (so the old \"network byte order\" was already improper here, but this is significantly worse).\nYou could say something like :\n\n  an int coding for an IPv4 address by packing its individual bytes into the int, lower-order to higher-order.\n\n\nNote that the implementation however is fine ; what the code does is indeed reversing the bytes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 70,
        "endLine": 130,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "4248be404a018db04856031425809eac911b8e24",
